    "cost_closing_html":  "About \u003cstrong\u003e$2.72 a bowl\u003c/strong\u003e (at everyday cost). A block of achiote paste costs a few dollars, lasts through several batches, and does flavor work you cannot buy any other way.",
    "shop_smart":  [
                       "\u003cstrong\u003eAchiote paste is the whole flavor and it is cheap.\u003c/strong\u003e Look for the small red brick in the Hispanic aisle. One block seasons this batch and several more after it, so the per serving cost is tiny.",
                       "\u003cstrong\u003eOrange juice, vinegar and lime stand in for sour orange.\u003c/strong\u003e Real sour orange is hard to find outside a Latin market. This combination is what every cook in the States uses and it costs pennies.",
